[38;5;231m⏺[39m This looks bounded: it's a change to one page that already exists. So I'll give you a short design here in chat rather
  than write a spec. Tell me if you'd rather I treat it as bigger.

  I found three existing problems on the page that affect this work. I haven't changed anything yet.

  - [1mJavaScript off:[0m the table rows are created entirely by [38;5;153mactivity.js[39m, so with JavaScript disabled the table is empty.
    That already breaks the rule in NOTES.md that content must work without JavaScript.
  - [1mRaw CSS values:[0m [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m uses raw hex and px values instead of the guideline tokens.
  - [1mNo time zone:[0m the When column shows local times with no time zone label.

  I'll ask you about each of these separately later on.

  The first question is where the filter controls go, and that's easier to show than describe. I've opened a browser tab
  with three wireframes: [94m]8;id=1f6vo4w;http://localhost:61222/?key=eae0abd44a4ebc57c8cefccbf2a72fce6cf7ebc8d9efa5c69edf6e6f64b2c9bd\http://localhost:61222/?key=eae0abd44a4ebc57c8cefccbf2a72fce6cf7ebc8d9efa5c69edf6e6f64b2c9bd[39m]8;;\.
  It uses a lot of tokens, so say so if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  - [1mA. Filter bar:[0m labeled controls always visible above the table, with a "Showing 4 of 45 events" count line.
  - [1mB. Shortcut + Select:[0m the same bar, plus a "Show failed sign-ins" button. Failed sign-ins are what every support
    ticket so far has been about.
  - [1mC. Popover:[0m a Filters button opens the controls, and active filters show as removable tags. It's tidier but takes an
    extra click and more code.

  I recommend B. It puts the most-requested case one click away and costs little more than A.

  Which placement do you want? You can click one in the browser or answer here.

  The companion stores its files in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo. There's no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet, so that folder should be
  ignored before anything gets committed.

